{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/pulls/4508","id":1366394028,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAU0OSs5RcYSs","html_url":"https://github.com/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/pull/4508","diff_url":"https://github.com/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/pull/4508.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/pull/4508.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/issues/4508","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/pulls/4508/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/pulls/4508/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/issues/4508/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/statuses/5ee984b3382c5c32ba4f2490a9db6313c6d3a20f","number":4508,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Batch and pipeline multiple Redis calls together","user":{"login":"Woellchen","id":1310072,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMTAwNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1310072?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Woellchen","html_url":"https://github.com/Woellchen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Woellchen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Woellchen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Woellchen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Woellchen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Woellchen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Woellchen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Woellchen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Woellchen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Woellchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"# What problem are we solving?\r\nWhen using Redis store there are a lot of single commands sent to Redis sequentially. This causes many round trips and network IO wait.\r\nFor example for directories this produces a GET command for each child in the directory. Imagine a folder with a million files, it would sequentially execute 1 million GET commands.\r\n\r\n\r\n# How are we solving the problem?\r\nUsing the client-side pipelining feature to send all commands and get all their results in a single roundtrip.\r\nThis is implemented for `redis2` stores. If you like the idea I can go ahead and change the other redis stores as well.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n# How is the PR tested?\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n# Checks\r\n- [ ] I have added unit tests if possible.\r\n- [ ] I will add related wiki document changes and link to this PR after merging.\r\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2023-05-26T13:52:46Z","updated_at":"2026-09-21T06:35:26Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"innogames:improve_redis_performance","ref":"improve_redis_performance","repo":{"id":521647496,"node_id":"R_kgDOHxe1iA","name":"seaweedfs","full_name":"innogames/seaweedfs","owner":{"login":"innogames","id":1314968,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjEzMTQ5Njg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1314968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/innogames","html_url":"https://github.com/innogames","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/innogames/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/innogames/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/innogames/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/innogames/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/innogames/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/innogames/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/innogames/repos","events_url":"https://api.githu